  "title": "Calorie estimates: handfuls, glugs, knobs, shots and scoops",
  "description": "30 lines (22 pipeline fixtures, 4 Paprika, 4 snapshots) use informal measures. \
Handfuls: \"1 large handful cilantro\", \"2 large handful spinach\", \"2-3 large handful fresh spinach\", \"1 small handful mint leaves\", \"2 big handfuls of chopped kale\", \"4-5 big handfuls of kale\": the model-estimated \"handful\" weight already exists for several of these foods (estimated_weights.json), but a sized handful (large/small/big) misses it; read a sized handful as a handful (or cite a size factor). \
Glugs of oil: \"2 glugs of olive oil\" x3, \"1 to 2 glugs olive oil\" x3, \"1 glug of olive oil per egg\" x3, \"1 glug olive oil or cooking fat\": a glug is roughly a tablespoon (find a cited convention). \"1-2 good knob butter\" (a knob of butter is about a tablespoon). \
Shots: \"1/2 shot espresso\" (1 fl oz, USDA lists a shot of espresso), \"2 to 3 really good shots hot sauce\" x3 (a dash-like measure; maybe 1 tsp). \
Scoops: \"2/4 scoop vanilla ice cream\" (a scoop is about 1/2 cup; USDA ice cream has portions), \"1 scoop protein powder\" (varies by brand; likely leave unknown). \
Measure with make ingredient-catalog-audit (Unsupported quantity unit, all three corpora) and, once blocked-ingredient-burndown-from-prod lands, the prod report; make pipeline should produce only data/ingredient-catalog-audit.md and fixture-category diffs. \
Server-side only (ramekin-core nutrition), so no web or iOS change. \
Split out of the retired p3-nutrition-remaining-count-units (owner, 2026-10-24: whole groups per PR, never one ingredient).",
